                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A code thread is one card, as on GitHub: the code and the comments, then a band with your avatar and “Reply…”, then a band with Resolve. Clicking “Reply…” opens the same editor as the comment at the end of the thread (Write / Preview, the Markdown tools, Cancel with Esc and Reply with ⌘↵) in that band, inside the card; it is code review's own reply box, so ⌘↵ says what it does there: Reply, Add to draft while your review draft is open, or Start a review when your setting puts replies into a review first. Changed and left (Esc, J / K, another item), it asks before discarding, as an edit does. It grows downwards and nothing above it moves. Below, the resolved thread opened from its folded line: Resolved, the code and the comments, the reply field, and Unresolve next to who resolved it. If GitHub refuses a resolve, the band says why, next to the button. A thread can be focused (click it, or J / K once one is): J / K move between code threads and R opens the focused one's reply box.",
