        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "xIBhB",
          "name": "Row of screens",
          "gap": 80,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "U9JZ1",
              "name": "Slot · F13 · Every event in the thread",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 14,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "ajsIl",
                  "name": "Caption",
                  "width": 1440,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 4,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "PTudq",
                      "name": "Caption title",
                      "fill": "$fg",
                      "content": "F13 · Every event in the thread",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 15,
                      "fontWeight": "500"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "HADwB",
                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Every timeline event githq shows, drawn with Activity / Event. Left: pull requests, with the ones issues have too marked “issues too”. Right: events only an issue has. The chip at the right of a row says what it counts as when a fold hides it. Pull requests show no issue-only events, and issues show no pushes, reviews or CI. Of a project, GitHub reports only Status changes, with the person who made them; a change made by a project workflow (automated) has no person and says so. Marked as a duplicate is not shown: the close it comes with says it (“closed this as a duplicate of #12”).",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "lGxhL",
                  "name": "F13 · Every event in the thread",
                  "width": 1440,
                  "fill": "$bg-item",
                  "cornerRadius": 10,
                  "stroke": "$border",
                  "strokeWidth": 1,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 36,
                  "padding": 40,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "J0LXH",
                      "name": "Rules",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "gap": 32,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "frame",
                          "id": "DEcln",
                          "name": "One line per burst",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "layout": "vertical",
                          "gap": 6,
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "bIylM",
                              "name": "Title",
                              "fill": "$fg",
                              "content": "One line per burst",
                              "fontFamily": "$font",
                              "fontSize": 13,
                              "fontWeight": "600"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "fdTFK",
                              "name": "Text",
                              "fill": "$fg-2",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "Events by one person, straight after each other and within 10 minutes, share one line: the first event's badge, the newest time, the parts joined with “and” — “added storage sync and asked sofiab and dkim for a review”. Events of one kind merge their objects, in the order the kinds first came: one object keeps its title, several show their references only — “mentioned this in #14, #15, and #16”. An add and a remove of the same thing cancel out. Comments, reviews, code comments and pushes never merge. GitHub gives no push time: one author's commits in a row are one push, split where more than an hour passed between two of them.",
                              "lineHeight": 1.5,
                              "fontFamily": "$font",
                              "fontSize": 12.5,
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "frame",
                          "id": "w5ya7",
                          "name": "CI, failures only",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "layout": "vertical",
                          "gap": 6,
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "oCEFu",
                              "name": "Title",
                              "fill": "$fg",
                              "content": "CI, failures only",
                              "fontFamily": "$font",
                              "fontSize": 13,
                              "fontWeight": "600"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "n0ntVn",
                              "name": "Text",
                              "fill": "$fg-2",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "The CI event appears once the checks on a pull request's newest commit finish and at least one failed: “CI 2 of 9 checks failed on e81f0a3: e2e, typecheck”, with “CI” where a person would be and no avatar. Only the newest run of each check counts, and a cancelled run is not a failure. Passing or running checks add no event; the commit's own dot in its push shows them. A later green run adds nothing either: the next push's dots say so.",
                              "lineHeight": 1.5,
                              "fontFamily": "$font",
                              "fontSize": 12.5,
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "frame",
                          "id": "fL7p4",
                          "name": "In a fold",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "layout": "vertical",
                          "gap": 6,
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "bjt1r",
                              "name": "Title",
                              "fill": "$fg",
                              "content": "In a fold",
                              "fontFamily": "$font",
                              "fontSize": 13,
                              "fontWeight": "600"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "F5ti1",
                              "name": "Text",
                              "fill": "$fg-2",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "A folded middle counts what it hides in three groups: commits (every commit of the pushes in it), comments (comments, reviews and code comments) and other events (every other event on this screen; the close GitHub adds to a merge is not one). The numbers are GitHub's own counts, so they add up to what expanding shows.",
                              "lineHeight": 1.5,
                              "fontFamily": "$font",
                              "fontSize": 12.5,
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "frame",
                          "id": "S8E1CJ",
                          "name": "Never shown",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "layout": "vertical",
                          "gap": 6,
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "g00GK",
                              "name": "Title",
                              "fill": "$fg",
                              "content": "Never shown",
                              "fontFamily": "$font",
                              "fontSize": 13,
                              "fontWeight": "600"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "nBP2d",
                              "name": "Text",
                              "fill": "$fg-2",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
