                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A review is one card: the reviewer's avatar in the gutter, the verdict in its head (approved green, changes requested red, “reviewed” for comments only), the summary, then its code threads. Without a summary the card holds just the threads; with no summary and a single thread GitHub can't tell it from a comment posted on its own, so it reads as a code comment. A dismissed review folds to its head, “Show review” opens it, and the dismissal follows as an event. Your own pending review sits at the end of the thread, above the composer, with the same band as in code review (“Submit review…” ⇧S, “Others can't see them until you submit.”) and its dialogs; nobody else sees it. A thread whose lines changed since says “Outdated” and keeps the old lines; unresolved it stays open, resolved it folds like any other.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
