              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 14,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "cIs13",
                  "name": "Caption",
                  "width": 1600,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 4,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "LXQlc",
                      "name": "Caption title",
                      "fill": "$fg",
                      "content": "F15 · A comment's ⋯ menu, and editing in place",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 15,
                      "fontWeight": "500"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "o9BXr",
                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "⋯ in a comment's head (or right-clicking the card outside its text — on the text itself the browser's menu stays, as everywhere GitHub's rendering shows) opens its menu: Edit, Quote reply, Copy link, Delete…. Edit turns the card into the editor where it stands, with its text: Cancel (Esc) puts the card back unchanged, or, once the text was changed, first asks in the footer: Keep editing (Esc) or Discard (↵); J / K, opening another item or closing it ask the same, and Discard then goes where you were going; an unchanged edit closes without a question, Update comment (⌘↵; Update description on the description) saves it, and the head then says “· edited”; if GitHub refuses, a toast says so and the editor opens again with your text. Quote reply puts the text, quoted, into the composer at the end and scrolls there. Copy link copies the comment's github.com link, quietly, as everywhere in githq. Delete… asks once, since GitHub keeps no copy. Edit and Delete are offered on your own comments, and on anyone's where you can write to the repository; otherwise the menu has Quote reply and Copy link. The description card has the same menu, without Delete.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
