                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The composer never waits: a comment can be written at once. The description, the comments and the events come together, in the item's detail, so the first time an item is opened before its detail is on this device (an item from outside what you track, or one the first sync hasn't reached) all of them are missing. Then the rail shows how many comments the item's row knows of and a skeleton in their shape, its first card standing for the description (left); on later opens they come from the local copy with no skeleton, and a read that fails then changes nothing on screen. With nothing after the description, the rail runs from it straight to the composer (middle). If GitHub can't be reached or refuses the first read, one line on the rail says so, with Try again and Open on GitHub (right). The Freshness screen “3d · item's comments still loading” uses the skeleton.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
