              "name": "Group title",
              "fill": "$fg",
              "content": "Searching GitHub for a repository",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 22,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Anrxt",
              "name": "Group note",
              "fill": "$fg-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "\"Search repositories…\" is a command like any other, and its submenu is the only place the menu asks GitHub: it sends what is typed, once typing pauses and from two characters, to GitHub's repository search, as github.com's search does. Public repositories and the private ones the user can see. Enter opens the repository's screen (J5). The top level goes on matching only what is kept here. Decision: D34.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "DYjbN",
          "name": "Row of screens · Search repositories",
          "gap": 80,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "Y49D5S",
              "name": "Slot · E6 · ⌘K on an untracked repository · Track repository",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 14,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "AEYT8",
                  "name": "Caption",
                  "width": 1440,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 4,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "ZNwVt",
                      "name": "Caption title",
                      "fill": "$fg",
                      "content": "E6 · ⌘K on an untracked repository · Track repository",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 15,
                      "fontWeight": "500"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "LZy1y",
                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Tracking also starts here (D34): \"Track repository\" shows only while the screen's repository is not tracked, as the last line of the group under its name (D32), so a plain Enter cannot start it. It starts the usual first download and leaves the rows on screen. A tracked repository has no such line, and \"Stop tracking\" stays in the sidebar's menu (D32). \"Search repositories…\" is in App on every screen. Neither has a button outside the menu. Go to is cut to two lines here; the list scrolls.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
