                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Opens at once from the row, already in the layout it keeps: the settings' methods 1 2 3, the checks' chevron (inactive until the read) and C Checks. A small loader beside the commit title says GitHub's message is on its way; when it arrives it opens below with Reveal, and nothing opens when there's no message (rebase, an empty body). The small “Reading” is the only other sign. ⌘↵ already works; GitHub then writes the default text. E waits for the proposal.",
