            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "Nn6ry",
              "name": "Slot · W1 · Sidebar states",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 14,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "x6Xul",
                  "name": "Caption",
                  "width": 1724,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 4,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "B45ld",
                      "name": "Caption title",
                      "fill": "$fg",
                      "content": "W1 · The sidebar: total and marker, expanded and on the rail",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 15,
                      "fontWeight": "500"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "GWKWz",
                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A marker can stay on for weeks, so it never moves, pulses or grows. It has two levels, computed from GitHub's data with nothing stored: bright for a break younger than 24 hours, quiet after that. It stays red either way and never goes away until a run passes. The marker sits on the repository's icon, so markers line up in one column and the open-items count beside the name stays. The Broken workflows entry is contextual: it appears only while at least one workflow is known to be broken, and while its own screen is open, where with nothing broken it reads 0, or – while something isn't read yet (W2b, W21). So the sidebar carries no idle row. With nothing broken, or nothing known yet, the screen is still one ⌘K away.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
