                      "fontWeight": "500"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "RCiX2",
                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "/ or ⌘F, because the browser's own find can't see lines that aren't drawn. Plain text, in smart case: all lower case ignores case, a capital makes it exact; no regex or case toggle. Search runs over the whole job at once, folded steps included: they show their match count, the job its total beside its time, and landing on a match opens its step. This match is the actual cause, 232 lines above the marker, which only said “exit code 1”. The hints along the bottom follow the focus. Shown here, with the field focused and its letters typed: only ↵ Next match and ⇧↵ Previous. With the focus out of the field: N Next match, ⇧N Previous, E Error, ⇧J ⇧K Step, ⌥J ⌥K Job, Y Copy link to line, O GitHub, ? All keys. Tab shows only the matching lines, Esc closes and returns to where you were.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
