                      "content": "A re-run lands here: the run changes to running and the workflow stays broken until it finishes. “· attempt 2” sits with the event, past the first attempt, and “started 1m ago” counts from the latest start, not the run's creation. Steps show their status. A running job's log can't be streamed, so the pane says so and points to GitHub, and it opens here by itself when the job finishes. Jobs that have finished already have their logs. A job still waiting says “{job} hasn't started yet”, detail “status: queued”.",
