                      "id": "i4V1q",
                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The repository is on the default, and Release failed on the tag v0.1.0-rc.3. Its row sits under No alerts and says why in its own words: the ref it failed on, and that it has no alerts. On a branch it reads “Failing on a branch without alerts”; with no ref known, “Failing without alerts”. The group header says what to do about it, and the Alerts bar above the list shows what does alert, with Alert settings and P, from any row. P opens the repository's settings (T16) on Workflow alerts; on a row without alerts it lands on the add field, so v* is two keystrokes away (W11). Esc comes back to this row. Deploy shows a break's first minute: “Broke just now”, “failed just now”.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
