            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Vtt0e",
              "name": "Group note",
              "fill": "$fg-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "One screen with a column of six sections, as the repository's column layout: Repositories, Projects, Display, Code review, Sync settings, Account. Keys 1 to 6 switch between them, and it opens from the menu on the signed-in user, the command menu or the , key. It is the only place to start tracking. Repositories and Projects list only what is tracked, grouped by owner, each row opening its own settings page (T16 for a repository) and untracked from the row; adding is a separate step, a picker opened with Track repositories or Track projects (T18–T22; first sign-in keeps its chooser, G2). The account stays a section rather than a page of its own, so the user menu needs one entry and there is one place to look. An organisation that hides its private data is flagged in the picker and in Account. Where settings are saved shows in the status bar, not on the page.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
