                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Track repositories (A) or a group's Track more opens the first sign-in chooser (G2) in a modal, so choosing what to track looks and works the same both times: owners on the left with tracked / all counts and, under them, \"Missing an organisation?\" with Grant access on GitHub (the same link as G8; the column is the component Track / Owner filter, so first sign-in G2 shows it too), the filter (/) and sort above the list, repositories grouped by owner. Tracked repositories show with a grey, fixed tick and \"tracked\", so the list answers \"is it already in?\"; an owner whose every repository is tracked folds to its header. A tick here only selects; nothing changes until Track 2 repositories (⌘↵). Esc or Cancel closes it without asking. Shown: opened with Track repositories, two picked. Keys: J and K move, Space ticks, / filters, ⌘↵ tracks, Esc closes.",
