                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "k0gK3I",
                      "name": "Caption title",
                      "fill": "$fg",
                      "content": "T16 · Settings · A repository's settings",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 15,
                      "fontWeight": "500"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "y3Dttd",
                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Every per-repository setting on one page: Settings › Repositories › owner/name. It opens with Enter on a tracked row in Repositories (G8), with Settings in the repository's menu, and with P from its Workflows section, which lands on Workflow alerts with its first row selected; Esc goes back where it came from. Sections stack, each with its name and what it changes on the left and its controls on the right, so new settings are new sections. Workflow alerts save as they change, like every edit in the app; Untrack works as on the repository's row in Repositories. Shown: only the default branch alerts, its switch selected. It is a switch with GitHub's name for the branch, not a pattern, so it has no edit or remove. Below the list, the branches and tags githq has seen runs on that raise no alert, so the reason a failure lit nothing is on the screen. Keys: J and K move, Space switches the default branch, Enter edits a pattern, A adds one, ⌫ removes one, Esc goes back.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
