            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ShEcf",
              "name": "Group note",
              "fill": "$fg-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Drawn in the tabs layout. One repository with a few branches (fitloop/webapp) and one with many (nuxt/nuxt, 67 branches, 339 tags). A row reads left to right: its place in the graph, the branches and tags at it, the headline, then right after it the pull request and its CI; the author (avatar and name) and the age are aligned at the right edge. Rows alternate with a very faint stripe, so a dot far to the left is easy to follow to its row. The default branch runs on the left in a lighter grey; a merge is a hollow dot with a dimmed headline. A divider between the graph and the rows can be dragged; lanes that don't fit fold.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
