                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The divider shows a grip on hover and the cursor turns to a resize arrow. While dragging, a small label says how many lanes fit of how many there are. The width is a share of the pane, so it scales with the window, and it is remembered on this device like a panel's width; a double-click on the divider goes back to the default. From the keyboard, ← and → change it by a lane, with the same label, and ↵ goes back to the default. The rows keep at least 240 px, so in a narrow pane not every lane may fit.",
