              "content": "3 · The branch and tag list",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 22,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "k9veH",
              "name": "Group note",
              "fill": "$fg-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "On the left of the graph in both layouts: in the tabs layout under the header, always there on a wide window, and below about 1200 px it folds away and B opens it over the graph from the left; in the column layout, the column's lower part. Every branch and tag on GitHub, the default branch first, then branches and tags newest first, each with its pull request and CI where it has them; the newest twenty of each are drawn and the rest counted. B puts the cursor in its filter; typing narrows both groups; ↵ or a click scrolls the graph to the commit, selects it there and goes back to the graph. The graph is never narrowed to one branch.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
