                      "content": "The moment before anything is typed. Pressing a line number opens the box on that line; dragging along the numbers grows the range, the lines tint as it goes and the box follows its last line. ⇧click on a second number does the same in one move, and ⇧↓ adds a line from the diff or from a box still empty (with text in it, ⇧↓ selects the text). A range stays on one side of the diff and stops at a gap, since what the reader hasn't seen isn't commented on. A click with no drag is a comment on that one line (CR70).",
