                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "As github.com: in the gutter, ↓ shows 20 lines below the hunk above and ↑ 20 above the hunk below; a gap of 20 or fewer has one ↕ for all of it. A click on the rest of the row shows 20 toward the nearest hunk, the one on the reading line's side (D44), and hovering the row lights the arrow it will take. The enclosing declaration sits in the row only when it's a real one; no hunk header, since our hunks aren't git's (D6). Top of the file has only ↑, the end only ↓. E expands the gap nearest the reading line, 20 toward its hunk each time it's pressed; \"Show all hidden lines\" in the command menu opens all of it.",
