                      "content": "The file V, Space and C act on has a faintly tinted header with an accent chevron, and its block's edge in accent; pinned or in place, expanded, collapsed or viewed alike. It's the file crossing the reading line, a third down under the pinned header, which is never drawn (purple here only as an annotation); a click, [ ], the file list or V moving on holds it until it leaves the screen or you scroll a fair way. C comments on this file's line at the reading line, or on its line nearest to it while the file is held off the line, so C never lands in another file than V and Space.",
