                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "B348v",
                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Once a file's patch is in (GET …/pulls/{n}/files, a separate request, 100 files a page), it decides the placeholder. (a) No patch and 0/0 lines: a binary file shows its final note; a pure rename (RENAMED, 0/0) says \"Renamed, no changes\". No bars, nothing shrinks. (b) A file with a patch draws its bars in the real hunk layout with their line numbers, the bars starting where the code will, its gap rows in place with their counts; in split a changed line is one row with both sides. The patch says which lines are added and deleted, so those bars take the line's tint. Close, not exact: our diff is not git's (D6), and D7's anchor absorbs a few rows' difference. \"Too large\" isn't in the patch (CR116).",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 12.5,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
