                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The moment before CR60. The list has come in one GraphQL request, with every path, change type and count of added and deleted lines; the patches are a separate request, 100 files a page, and nothing else is here yet. So every file is its header and D38's grey bars, as many as its added and deleted lines: a guess, no tint, no gap rows. A file with 0/0 lines is only its header until its patch page says binary or renamed. As each page lands its files' bars take the hunk layout and tint (CR111); a difference in height above the reading line goes into the scroll position (D7), so what you look at holds.",
