                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "schema.json changed 4 lines but weighs 4.2 MB. Its patch has the hunks, so at first it draws tinted bars like any file (CR111). Whether it's past the size githq diffs (D35) is known only when its blob arrives (byteSize); then the bars turn into the note, the block shrinks, and D7's anchor keeps what you read in place. When GitHub sent no patch because the diff itself is too big, the bars are grey and sized from the counts (CR88), and turn into the note the same way.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 12.5,
