                  "width": 1600,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 4,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "RDeI9",
                      "name": "Caption title",
                      "fill": "$fg",
                      "content": "I4 · The composer's states",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 15,
                      "fontWeight": "500"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "L5oEi3",
                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The composer at the end of an issue's or a pull request's thread. Closing an issue asks for a reason: ⇧X closes as completed, the chevron opens the reasons. Once text is typed the close button posts it, then closes (“Close with comment”); ⇧X and the item menu's close do the same. A closed item offers Reopen, a merged pull request offers no close button, and where you can't comment the editor gives way to one quiet line saying why. A sent comment shows at once in the thread as a new card, dimmed until GitHub has it; if GitHub refuses it, the card stays with its text, Retry and Discard, and no toast: the card says it. @ and # open a suggestion list at the caret, kept inside the item: @ lists the thread's people first, then the repository's; # lists the repository's issues and pull requests from this device when it's tracked, else from GitHub's search once typing pauses, never the item itself. ↑↓ move, ↵ or Tab inserts, Esc closes the list and leaves the item open; in a modal the first Esc leaves the box, the next closes the item. The reasons are completed and not planned; Close as duplicate is left out for now, because it needs an issue picker, and comes later.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
